//
// An automation is a versioned definition that makes the Core create an
// ordinary task when a trigger fires. These messages manage definitions, the
// owner's enable approval, the kill switches and the run history, and carry a
// trigger event in. A trigger never produces anything but `CreateTask` and
// `StartTask` for a principal under a ceiling (the Core issues those itself);
